# SyncBridge — Global Project Rules

Personal-use app: **1 user**, **max 5 devices** (MacBook, Android, iPhone, Web).  
Infra: **1 VPS**, **≤1 GB RAM**, **Go monolith**, **PostgreSQL**, **local filesystem**.

## Do NOT build

Multi-user, email/username login, registration, password reset, OAuth/SSO/LDAP, E2E encryption / key management, Redis/Kafka/RabbitMQ/Elasticsearch/Kubernetes/microservices.  
**Do not default to MinIO or S3** — S3 only behind an optional feature flag.

## Stack (only)

Go monolith · PostgreSQL · WebSocket · WebRTC · local filesystem at `/opt/syncbridge/storage/`

```
/opt/syncbridge/storage/
  clipboard/  images/  screenshots/  files/  temp/  pinned/
```

## Authentication

- **Single master PIN**: `070901` (stored in `settings.master_pin`)
- No username, email, registration, or password reset
- **Backend validates PIN** — never trust frontend-only checks
- Successful PIN → **trust device 7 days** (no PIN prompt within window)
- After 7 days → ask for PIN again

## Data retention

| Content | Unpinned lifetime |
|---------|-------------------|
| Clipboard, images, screenshots | 2 hours |
| Files | Delete after **successful delivery**, else 2 hours |

**Pinned**: never auto-delete; permanent; synced across devices.  
UI: **Temporary Section** + **Pinned Section** (📌 Pin / Unpin on every item).

## Storage limits

- Unpinned content: **max 1 GB total** — delete **oldest unpinned first** when exceeded
- Pinned content: never auto-deleted

## Transfer priority

1. Same Wi-Fi direct (mDNS + WebRTC) — never upload unnecessarily on LAN
2. Internet WebRTC
3. TURN relay
4. Cloud relay (last resort)

**Large files**

| Size | Rule |
|------|------|
| ≤100 MB | Cloud relay allowed |
| 100 MB–1 GB | Direct first; cloud fallback OK |
| >1 GB | **Never auto cloud upload** — on failure show: Retry Direct / Wait for Wi-Fi / Upload Anyway |

## Performance targets

| Metric | Target |
|--------|--------|
| Backend idle RAM | <100 MB |
| Backend startup | <2 s |
| Clipboard (Wi-Fi) | <500 ms |
| Clipboard (cloud) | <2 s |

## Implementation principle

Choose the **simplest** implementation that meets requirements.  
Feel like **Universal Clipboard + AirDrop + history** — fast, simple, reliable, low RAM/disk, minimal config.
